Engine-data round (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): synthetic fixtures for frame generation with DCS's own data, since the live
R71 captures are gone. tests/fg_engine_data.inc (XRFG_TEST_FG_ENGINE_DATA=1, ctest xrfg_d3d12_fg_engine_data, NVIDIA
hardware, skipped without) draws a flight scene at the previous frame, the current one and halfway (the truth): sky and
terrain rolling 1.5 degrees a pair, power lines nearer than the terrain, an aircraft over the terrain and one in the sky
(DCS's model class), the cockpit's strut and panel (mask), by day and by night (a quarter of the light), with and
without effects that DCS draws after its G-buffer (a still HUD, a drifting smoke puff, sparks: no MVs). Each frame
carries what the engine module exports: MVs and the class atlas at the render resolution (10 output pixels a texel: the
periphery's MVs where the composed image shows the focus view; 2: the focus view's own) and the cockpit mask. Every
composition (the optical flow alone, along the MVs) is measured against the truth in sRGB units per region: models,
what a model uncovers or covers (behind / ahead of it), wires, the cockpit's edge, HUD, smoke, particles, the rest, all;
and the share composed along the MVs. Options in the variable's value: "fast" (the Fast preset), "cell" (the MV texel
against the resample's cell, with XRFG_TEST_DCS_MOTION_CELL forcing the cell: tests only), "x4" (2560 x 1920),
"smooth" (a 4-degree roll over a nearly flat sky). The product is unchanged (the cell override reads a test variable).
